ng which is to go into the agent MD every time the model does something wrong and add something small to it saying \"Don't do this again.\" And that does help It does work But at some point you have to reflect and reali", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/theo/status/2092372584180687279#t=2214", "end": 2332.485, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "906a295b35e70923e5ba850dda80a2bb9faa66f4c683456101e173732bb04307", "start": 2214.126, "text": "me at things that my slop code does I add them here to keep steering in the direction that makes Julius happy He really likes the adapter boundary being where complexity lives so that the orchestration can be really simple and the UI can be", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}], "current_topic": "Social Media Research", "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpts": [{"deep_link": "https://x.com/theo/status/2092372584180687279#t=118", "end": 238.835, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "97fd205a2787e4e02a51e55e24a5b2ed0df2b5cc17dcacff598a45f0e2b03285", "start": 118.979, "text": "Anthropic, Cursor And thinking machines all have in common because it's not just that they're trying to make models is that they all use today's sponsor WorkOS. You might be confused why so many big companies are choosing to use a product l", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/theo/status/2092372584180687279#t=709", "end": 827.78, "evidence_kind": "timed_clip", "excerpt_id": "d7034326e61d548e650f759d452222f268ba5c978dc56f7c3e0575a77ebf4886", "start": 709.041, "text": "Well, it pulls down a bunch of JSON files some of which it loads in a context but if it pulls too much And basic capping it and say like \"Hey, I showed you three items but I downloaded 52 into this JSON file If I think the structure looks c", "timing": "source_cues", "truncated": true}, {"deep_link": "https://x.com/theo/status/2092372584180687279#t=1223", "end": 1321.986, "evidence_kind": 